From 4a33ecdc33bbbe9c7cdf4f5ec5517208e598604a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liberodark <liberodark@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: add Aura Semiconductor AU4562 driver

The AU4562 is a PMBus controlled dual-output multiphase VR controller.
Select the output with PAGE and program VOUT_COMMAND, a 12-bit value in
5 mV steps (0x6c = 540 mV .. 0xdc = 1100 mV). The outputs are enabled by
hardware and stay on, so only the voltage is exposed, as a linear
selector range through the regulator core helpers.

PAGE is a shared selector: a PAGE write and the VOUT_COMMAND read-modify-
write that follows are done with the bus segment locked, so that nothing
else on the bus can redirect the access to the other output. Before an
output is registered, the value firmware left in VOUT_COMMAND is checked
to be inside the window this encoding covers; anything else is refused
rather than decoded with the wrong scale. VOUT_MODE is logged for
reference.

It feeds the CPU cluster rails of SpacemiT K3 boards, where the K3
firmware programs it the same way before handing over to the kernel.

Signed-off-by: liberodark <liberodark@gmail.com>
---
